"""W0-2A RBAC permission catalog — single source of truth (§15.1).

Generated literally from the owner-approved architecture document
docs/architecture/W0-2A_RBAC_OFFLINE_SECURITY_DESIGN_DRAFT.md
(§15/§15A) at commit e0d7db4505b7c04b1093c07e953aa4b1a3944f1d
(document blob 5f5f8f6709cfcacab0fa16f6e1e3bcdb448a2430).

This module is the ONLY authority for catalog content: the W0-2A seed
migration 0003 writes rows from SECURITY_PERMISSION_CATALOG, and the
database system check (security.checks) fails loudly on any drift
between this registry and the seeded security.Permission rows (§15.1).

Rules encoded here (§15.1):
- No wildcard keys; every key is a literal ``domain.resource.action``
  matching PERMISSION_KEY_REGEX.
- Every entry carries an explicit scope_policy: NONE, WAREHOUSE_REQUIRED,
  OBJECT_REQUIRED, or the design-time fail-closed marker UNRESOLVED.
  Missing/unrecognized metadata is a configuration error that fails
  closed; it MUST NOT default to NONE.
- The ten UNRESOLVED keys (documents.document.* 9 + sales.document.approve)
  are not seedable and are seeded to no one (§15.4).
- Status vocabulary: ENDPOINT (mounted API today), SERVICE (service-layer
  chokepoint today), MATRIX (owner-approved matrix only), RESERVED (OD-6
  dependency), UNRESOLVED (insufficient grounding).
- GM seed rule: GM is seeded with every key whose status is ENDPOINT,
  SERVICE, or MATRIX — the protected GM capability set (152 keys).

The module intentionally has NO Django imports: it is pure data plus
pure-Python validation so it can be imported anywhere, including inside
data migrations and system checks.
"""

